A||||11||docprego||Should I buy this 88 GT?||||1||
Z||000000||docprego||03-28-2001||03:20 AM||||I found a White 88 GT that I went to look at.  The car had 119K on the odometer when a new engine was put in about a year ago.  Now the car has 124K on the odometer, so it had only seen about 5K miles since the new engine went in.  There is 6 months/13,000 miles remaining on the new engines warranty.  Car is loaded with power everything, sunroof and factory sub.<P>The car is the cleanest, best conditin GT I have ever personally seen.  Not a single wear mark on the interior.  The only flaw at all is a small crack in the door right behind the passenger mirror that was the result of a break in attempt.  It is not obvious unless you look behind the mirror, as it is just at the top of the door at the point where the window starts).  Picture putting a crow bar down into the window channel from the outside just behind the mirror and then pulling the top of the crow bar towards you, you can picture the damage I am referring to then.  Other than that (oh yeah and 1 small crack in the passenger sail window) the car is mint.<P>I would buy this car in a second if it were not for the mileage before the engine replacement and the engine replacement itself.  <P>Another issue, I am told the heater core is disconnected and needs to be replaced.  I live in a 100 degree plus climate so I am not too worried about this.  But is there any other implications that this may result in?<P>Lastly, the left set of exhaust tips lies lower than the right.  The owner told me this happened after a leaking exhaust repair.  Can I get this adjusted to be even with the right set, or even bend it up myself?<P>Am I looking at this wrong, is this essentially a mint GT with the BONUS of a brand new engine?<P>Someone push me over the edge, convince me to buy this car!  Seller is asking $3800<P>Thanks for your patience reading this long winded message and appreciate any input,<BR>docprego<P>P.S.  Anyone familiar with bodywork have a ballpark estimate to fix the small crack where the passenger door is bent out ever so slightly jus at the top of the door where the window starts, right behind the passenger's mirror?||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierodave||03-28-2001||04:38 AM||||Go to Kelly blue book and look up the price it's going for right now!<BR>that should be enough to push you over the edge!  If not  wait a week, it will probably be sold!  That's a great price if the car is as you described.  any good body shop should be able to repair that spot for less than $200.00 <BR>replace the heater core  it's a $25.00 part and maybe at most a one hour Job if you have never done one before!<BR>If the sail window is a problem  get hold off 007 Doug  the fierowarehouse  he is a member here and he sells the repo sails that are x-lint  I know  I have gotten about 10 sets  lol<P>the exhaust tip clamp can be loosened and you can tip it to the right spot and reclamp it!<BR>have fun.......sounds like a great Car!<BR>FD<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||docprego||03-28-2001||11:16 AM||||Thanks, I guess I have a winner on my hands.  I am going to buy it today.  But first I am going to have a mechanic look at it and tell me of anything else that may need attention.<P>Anything in particular to be on the lookout for?<P>Thanks,<BR>docprego <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||03-28-2001||11:34 AM||||Sounds like a deal to me.  The exhaust tip thing is common, you can go to any exhaust shop and they fill fix it for you for 20 bucks.  Is it a 5 speed?  Gray or beechwood interior? Gold wheels?  Good find either way just curious.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Dingo||03-28-2001||11:46 AM||||I say buy it. You cant go off Kelly Blue book. You need to go off the price for your area. And it is also hard to tell someone if they are getting a good deal or not without actually seeing the car/truck etc. .  I am also into other types of vehicles and on other lists that serve that type of vehicle. I myself have been into cars since 1980 and can do most mechanical work on any of these vehicle with my eyes closed. I have a breif experience with Fieros only because I owned one for two years of my life and have always wanted to own another. My kids are getting to the age where we can finally buy another car without the thought of will it fit the family. Anyway back on subject. This sounds like a very good deal to me. The price sounds fair and the mileage for me would not be an issue being the motor is brand new. I would ask for recepts and also ask if they replaced any of the usual stuff while doing the motor. And always try and talk them down from the listed price. Doesnt hurt to barter even when they say the price is firm. Can't tell you how many times I have talked folks down from a firm price tag or have received extra items in the purchase only because I tried to talk them down. Not saying it will happen in your case but you never know unless you try. Good luck and let the group know how things went||||reg||1
Z||000005||docprego||03-28-2001||02:44 PM||||Jeff-<P>The car has the gray interior-absolutely mint condition-no rips!  1st Fiero I looked at with no tears on the drivers seat.<P>It has the black honeycomb wheels, was this common?<P>It is an automatic, perhaps my only dissapointment at all, I really wanted a 5 speed.  Oh well I see it as a small compromise, besides it does have the advantage of being able to be driven by my wife in a pinch.<P>Thanks for all the suggestions, I am definitely buying this car.<P>Will post a full report when I get it in my garage.<P>Mike<BR>(soon to be 88 White GT)<p>[This message has been edited by docprego (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||docprego||03-28-2001||11:09 PM||||I went to look at the car today, 1st time in daylight.  It stood up to the 1st night viewing well.<P>I found one touched up nick on the driver's door edge, that's it.<P>Peeked in the interior and noticed that the driver's seat had a control panel on it's right bolster, I guess I have power seats too!<P>Mechanic is inspecting it tommorow and I will be purchasing it right after that.<P>docprego <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indyellowgt||03-29-2001||12:49 AM||||LUCKY YOU!!<BR>The "Control panel" on the driver seat you referred to is the Lumbar seat option.Very rare indeed(88GT only!!..like 800ish made!!)<BR>Sounds like you have a great car on your hands.<BR>However,like other members have said,check into the "new motor" for solid proof,and I would suggest running a quick car-fax check on it too.Checking the usual areas for previous accident damage is a must too.<BR>Good luck!!<P>-Mark  88 yellow GT,lumbar too!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||docprego||03-29-2001||01:52 AM||||WOW!  I tripped and landed in front of a prize!  I can't believe it is 1 of 800 or so!<BR>I genuinely feel lucky.<P>I couldn't resist showing my wife the car tonight so we went over there and the seller graciously showed it to me for the 3rd time and my wife for the first time.<P>My wife was stunned.  She could not believe how sweet looking this car is.  On the way home she said it looked like a Lamborghini from the rear!<P>I started it up and let it run for about 2 minutes.  The idle seemed high to me.  I expected it to be in the 800 range, but it was in the 1200 range of the tach.  What is a normal idle for a V6 Fiero?  Is the idle a simple matter of having it adjusted?  The seller said it was sitting for the last 3 weeks undriven and that she also thought the idle was slightly high.<P>Well tomorrow is the big day.  Just for curiosity check out this web site <A HREF="http://www.inspectorauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.inspectorauto.com</A>  - they are doing my Fiero inspection tomorrow at 1pm.  Seems like a great service at a fair price.  They meet you at the car's location, thoroughly inspect it, appraise it and run a title history.<P>One last question.  If I want to replace the stock am/fm cassette which is still in the car with a CD player, can I still take advantage or the factory sub that the car has?  Is the factory sub any good?<P>Thanks for all of you input and for allowing my novellas.<P>docprego <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000009||mrfiero||03-29-2001||01:59 AM||||Sounds like a nice GT.  Send me the VIN number and I can run a carfax on it for you.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||docprego||03-29-2001||11:05 AM||||Thanks Mr. Fiero but I do not have the VIN, never wrote it down because my inspection today includes a title search in the fee.<P>docprego<P>P.S.  Today is the big day!||||reg||1
Z||000011||docprego||03-29-2001||11:13 PM||||I got it!!!!!!<P>The auto inspector gave it a clean bill of health and recommended that I buy the car, which of course I did!  He found virtually nothing wrong with the car, the worst thing was that the brakes were at 50% rear and 60% front, tires 60% rear and 75% front.<P><BR>I am psyched, that is the best looking vehicle I have ever had in my garage, it just looks nasty sitting in there!<P>It's in my garage right now, looking swwwwwwwwwwwwweeeeeeeeeeeeeeetttttttttttttt!<P>Just the drive home was so much fun, but now I realize I need a good stereo system, the front speakers buzz badly.  By buzz I mean they don't handle bass well at all.<P>What speakers are a drop in fit for the front and sail panel locations?<P>Should I keep the factory sub and how do I interface it with the rest of the system?<P>Thanks,<BR>docfiero, errr I mean docprego <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <P><BR>[This message has been edited by docprego (edited 03-29-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by docprego (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||1
